  "authoring": "Native pixel material and blade recipes extend the current grass palette and rooted-clump vocabulary. New blades use explicit root/tip/width/depth geometry; original packs are read only.",
  "notes": [
    "Ground motifs are designed clusters, not uniform per-pixel noise.",
    "All tile borders share the common base green for seamless composition.",
    "All tall-grass states preserve the same hard-alpha roots in rows26..28.",
    "Tall grass is visual, fully walkable and owned by a separate interactive layer."
  ]
